WEBVTT

00:08:58.826 --> 00:09:01.745
It’s part of our shared
social conversation and space.

00:09:01.787 --> 00:09:04.206
It’s something that belongs
to all of us in the UK,

00:09:04.248 --> 00:09:05.583
and we're very proud of it.

00:09:05.624 --> 00:09:10.004
So if you want welfare services
which address hardship,

00:09:10.045 --> 00:09:11.505
reduce inequality,

00:09:11.505 --> 00:09:14.425
are effective, efficient
and broadly liked,

00:09:14.425 --> 00:09:16.051
make them universal.

00:09:16.677 --> 00:09:21.557
"OK, I like universal services,
but how do we pay for this?"

00:09:21.599 --> 00:09:23.434
In a word, tax.

00:09:24.226 --> 00:09:26.687
Hardly reinventing the wheel, I know.

00:09:27.771 --> 00:09:31.317
In the United States, in the 1950s,
the top rate of tax was 90 percent.